IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `la-dates`
IMPORT `la-core`

-- Limitation Act 1969 (NSW) -- THE SEAT OF THE PERSON BRINGING THE CLAIM: the person injured or wronged (including
-- the person abused as a child), the personal representative suing for that person's estate, and the relatives suing
-- for the death. Every question is asked as that person would ask it, from facts that person can state; the court's
-- judgments are asked as conditions. The rules are in la-core.l4; this module restates none of them.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Based on content from the New South Wales Legislation website at 10 March 2025, via the Open Australian
-- Legal Corpus (version as at 16 June 2022). State of New South Wales, CC BY 4.0. See SOURCE-LICENSE.md. BASELINE
-- ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `The questions of the person bringing the claim`

-- Builds the core's record from the plain answers; every field is read by some rule.
GIVEN `my kind of claim` IS A `Kind of claim`
      `who is suing` IS A `Plaintiff`
      `the kind of abuse` IS A `Kind of abuse`
      `the day of the act or omission` IS A DATE
      `the injured person's date of birth` IS A DATE
      `the day the cause of action accrued` IS A DATE
      `the day the claim became discoverable by me` IS A DATE
      `the defendant was a parent or guardian or a close associate of one` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I had a capable parent or guardian while a minor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I was incapacitated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the incapacity began` IS A DATE
      `the incapacity has ended` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the incapacity ended` IS A DATE
      `I was a protected person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of death` IS A DATE
      `the deceased could discover the claim` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the deceased could discover it` IS A DATE
      `the day of appointment` IS A DATE
      `there was fraud or concealment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day it was discovered` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Claim facts`
`the facts from my answers` `my kind of claim` `who is suing` `the kind of abuse` `the day of the act or omission` `the injured person's date of birth` `the day the cause of action accrued` `the day the claim became discoverable by me` `the defendant was a parent or guardian or a close associate of one` `I had a capable parent or guardian while a minor` `I was incapacitated` `the day the incapacity began` `the incapacity has ended` `the day the incapacity ended` `I was a protected person` `the day of death` `the deceased could discover the claim` `the day the deceased could discover it` `the day of appointment` `there was fraud or concealment` `the day it was discovered` MEANS
    `Claim facts` WITH
        `the kind of claim` IS `my kind of claim`
        `the plaintiff` IS `who is suing`
        `the kind of abuse` IS `the kind of abuse`
        `the day of the act or omission` IS `the day of the act or omission`
        `the injured person's date of birth` IS `the injured person's date of birth`
        `the day the cause of action accrued` IS `the day the cause of action accrued`
        `the day the claim became discoverable by the plaintiff` IS `the day the claim became discoverable by me`
        `the defendant was a parent or guardian of the injured person, or a close associate of one` IS `the defendant was a parent or guardian or a close associate of one`
        `the injured person had a capable parent or guardian while a minor` IS `I had a capable parent or guardian while a minor`
        `the injured person was incapacitated` IS `I was incapacitated`
        `the day the incapacity began` IS `the day the incapacity began`
        `the incapacity has ended` IS `the incapacity has ended`
        `the day the incapacity ended` IS `the day the incapacity ended`
        `the injured person was a protected person while incapacitated` IS `I was a protected person`
        `the day of the death` IS `the day of death`
        `the deceased could discover the claim before the death` IS `the deceased could discover the claim`
        `the day the claim became discoverable by the deceased` IS `the day the deceased could discover it`
        `the day the personal representative was appointed` IS `the day of appointment`
        `there was fraud, deceit or concealment by the defendant` IS `there was fraud or concealment`
        `the day the fraud or concealment was or could have been discovered` IS `the day it was discovered`

§§ `Abuse suffered as a child (Part 1, s 6A; Schedule 5 Part 3)`
-- Situation: you were abused before you turned 18 (or you sue for the estate or as relatives of a person who was), and
-- want damages for the injury or the death.

@export Is there any time limit on my claim for damages for abuse I suffered as a child in New South Wales (Limitation Act 1969 s 6A)?
GIVEN `the kind of abuse` IS A `Kind of abuse` @desc The kind of abuse: sexual abuse; serious physical abuse; other abuse connected with sexual or serious physical abuse of you (by anyone), split by whether that sexual or serious physical abuse was also perpetrated before your 18th birthday; physical abuse that was not serious and not connected; other abuse not connected; or the injury did not result from abuse
      `my claim is for damages for injury or death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim is for damages relating to your personal injury (any disease or impairment of physical or mental condition), or to the death of the person abused
      `the abused person's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc The date of birth of the person who was abused
      `the day the abuse was perpetrated` IS A DATE @desc The day the abuse was perpetrated (the first day, if it went on over a period)
GIVETH A `Child abuse answer`
`Is there a time limit on my child abuse claim` MEANS
    `the s 6A answer for` `the kind of abuse` `with a personal injury claim` `my claim is for damages for injury or death` `born` `the abused person's date of birth` `abused on` `the day the abuse was perpetrated`

@export My child abuse claim was out of time, or an earlier action failed or was settled: can I sue now (Limitation Act 1969 s 6A, Schedule 5 cll 8-10)?
GIVEN `the kind of abuse` IS A `Kind of abuse` @desc The kind of abuse: sexual abuse; serious physical abuse; other abuse connected with sexual or serious physical abuse of you (by anyone), split by whether that sexual or serious physical abuse was also perpetrated before your 18th birthday; physical abuse that was not serious and not connected; other abuse not connected; or the injury did not result from abuse
      `my claim is for damages for injury or death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim is for damages relating to your personal injury (any disease or impairment of physical or mental condition), or to the death of the person abused
      `the abused person's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc The date of birth of the person who was abused
      `the day the abuse was perpetrated` IS A DATE @desc The day the abuse was perpetrated (the first day, if it went on over a period)
      `the earlier proceedings` IS AN `Earlier proceedings` @desc What happened before on this claim: no earlier action or judgment; an earlier action, with no judgment on the ground that the limitation period had expired; a judgment on the claim given or entered on that ground; a judgment against your lawyers for professional negligence given on the ground that a limitation period had expired; an agreement made before and in connection with such a judgment; or a settlement with no such judgment
GIVETH A `Previously barred answer`
`Can I sue now on my child abuse claim that was barred or judged before` MEANS
    `the Schedule 5 answer for` (`the s 6A answer for` `the kind of abuse` `with a personal injury claim` `my claim is for damages for injury or death` `born` `the abused person's date of birth` `abused on` `the day the abuse was perpetrated`) `after` `the earlier proceedings`

§§ `The time limit for my claim (Part 2, Part 3 Divisions 1 and 2)`

@export Which limitation period applies to my claim in New South Wales (Limitation Act 1969 ss 6A, 7, 14, 16-19, 50A-50E)?
GIVEN `my kind of claim` IS A `Kind of claim` @desc The kind of claim: damages for death or personal injury (any disease or impairment of physical or mental condition, however the claim is framed); damages or money in contract (not under a deed) or tort with no personal injury, or money recoverable under an enactment; a claim founded on a deed; a claim on a judgment; a penalty or forfeiture recoverable under an enactment; a claim for which another Act fixes the limitation period, such as a motor accident claim; or another kind of claim
      `who is suing` IS A `Plaintiff` @desc Who brings the claim: the person injured or wronged, suing for themselves; the personal representative (executor or administrator) of an injured person who has died, suing for the estate; or relatives suing for the death under the Compensation to Relatives Act 1897
      `the kind of abuse` IS A `Kind of abuse` @desc If the injury resulted from abuse, its kind: sexual abuse; serious physical abuse; other abuse connected with sexual or serious physical abuse (by anyone), split by whether that sexual or serious physical abuse was also perpetrated before the 18th birthday; physical abuse that was not serious and not connected; other abuse not connected; or the injury did not result from abuse
      `the day of the act or omission` IS A DATE @desc The day of the act or omission that caused the injury or death (for abuse, the day it was perpetrated, or the first day if over a period); for another claim, the day of the breach or wrong
      `the injured person's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc The date of birth of the person who was injured or wronged (yours, if you sue for yourself)
      `the day the cause of action accrued` IS A DATE @desc For a claim outside Division 6 (an act or omission before 6 December 2002, or a claim that is not for personal injury): the day the cause of action accrued, usually the day the damage was suffered; for a judgment, the day it became enforceable (any day otherwise)
      `the day the claim became discoverable by me` IS A DATE @desc For a personal injury claim: the first day you knew or ought to have known that the injury or death had occurred, that it was caused by the defendant's fault, and (for injury) that it was serious enough to justify suing; for a minor with a capable parent or guardian, what that parent or guardian knew or ought to have known counts
      `the defendant was a parent or guardian or a close associate of one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, at the time of the act or omission, the person you sue was the injured person's parent or guardian, or someone so close to a parent or guardian that the parent might be influenced not to sue them, or the child might be unwilling to tell the parent about it
      `I had a capable parent or guardian while a minor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, while the injured person was under 18, they had a parent or guardian who was not themselves under a disability
      `I was incapacitated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, after the time began to run, the injured person was for 28 days or more in a row incapable of, or substantially impeded in, managing their affairs about this claim, because of disease or impairment, restraint (including detention) or war
      `the day the incapacity began` IS A DATE @desc The day that incapacity began (any day otherwise)
      `the incapacity has ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that incapacity has ended
      `the day the incapacity ended` IS A DATE @desc The day the incapacity ended (any day otherwise)
      `I was a protected person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, during the incapacity, the injured person had a guardian (under the Guardianship Act 1987 or another law) or an order for management of their estate under the NSW Trustee and Guardian Act 2009 or the Guardianship Act 1987
      `the day of death` IS A DATE @desc For a claim by the estate or by relatives: the day the injured person died (any day otherwise)
      `the deceased could discover the claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a claim by the estate: whether the claim became discoverable by the person who died, before their death
      `the day the deceased could discover it` IS A DATE @desc The day the claim became discoverable by the person who died (any day otherwise)
      `the day of appointment` IS A DATE @desc For a claim by the estate: the day the personal representative (executor or administrator) was appointed (any day otherwise)
      `there was fraud or concealment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim is based on fraud or deceit by the person you sue, or that person fraudulently concealed the claim or who was liable
      `the day it was discovered` IS A DATE @desc The day you discovered the fraud, deceit or concealment, or could with reasonable diligence have discovered it (any day otherwise)
GIVETH A `Period answer`
`Which limitation period applies to my claim` MEANS
    `the period for` (`the facts from my answers` `my kind of claim` `who is suing` `the kind of abuse` `the day of the act or omission` `the injured person's date of birth` `the day the cause of action accrued` `the day the claim became discoverable by me` `the defendant was a parent or guardian or a close associate of one` `I had a capable parent or guardian while a minor` `I was incapacitated` `the day the incapacity began` `the incapacity has ended` `the day the incapacity ended` `I was a protected person` `the day of death` `the deceased could discover the claim` `the day the deceased could discover it` `the day of appointment` `there was fraud or concealment` `the day it was discovered`)

@export By when must I commence my action, counting discoverability, my childhood or incapacity, fraud or concealment, and the 30-year ultimate bar (Limitation Act 1969 ss 6A, 14, 16-19, 50C-50F, 51, 52, 55)?
GIVEN `my kind of claim` IS A `Kind of claim` @desc The kind of claim: damages for death or personal injury (any disease or impairment of physical or mental condition, however the claim is framed); damages or money in contract (not under a deed) or tort with no personal injury, or money recoverable under an enactment; a claim founded on a deed; a claim on a judgment; a penalty or forfeiture recoverable under an enactment; a claim for which another Act fixes the limitation period, such as a motor accident claim; or another kind of claim
      `who is suing` IS A `Plaintiff` @desc Who brings the claim: the person injured or wronged, suing for themselves; the personal representative (executor or administrator) of an injured person who has died, suing for the estate; or relatives suing for the death under the Compensation to Relatives Act 1897
      `the kind of abuse` IS A `Kind of abuse` @desc If the injury resulted from abuse, its kind: sexual abuse; serious physical abuse; other abuse connected with sexual or serious physical abuse (by anyone), split by whether that sexual or serious physical abuse was also perpetrated before the 18th birthday; physical abuse that was not serious and not connected; other abuse not connected; or the injury did not result from abuse
      `the day of the act or omission` IS A DATE @desc The day of the act or omission that caused the injury or death (for abuse, the day it was perpetrated, or the first day if over a period); for another claim, the day of the breach or wrong
      `the injured person's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc The date of birth of the person who was injured or wronged (yours, if you sue for yourself)
      `the day the cause of action accrued` IS A DATE @desc For a claim outside Division 6 (an act or omission before 6 December 2002, or a claim that is not for personal injury): the day the cause of action accrued, usually the day the damage was suffered; for a judgment, the day it became enforceable (any day otherwise)
      `the day the claim became discoverable by me` IS A DATE @desc For a personal injury claim: the first day you knew or ought to have known that the injury or death had occurred, that it was caused by the defendant's fault, and (for injury) that it was serious enough to justify suing; for a minor with a capable parent or guardian, what that parent or guardian knew or ought to have known counts
      `the defendant was a parent or guardian or a close associate of one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, at the time of the act or omission, the person you sue was the injured person's parent or guardian, or someone so close to a parent or guardian that the parent might be influenced not to sue them, or the child might be unwilling to tell the parent about it
      `I had a capable parent or guardian while a minor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, while the injured person was under 18, they had a parent or guardian who was not themselves under a disability
      `I was incapacitated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, after the time began to run, the injured person was for 28 days or more in a row incapable of, or substantially impeded in, managing their affairs about this claim, because of disease or impairment, restraint (including detention) or war
      `the day the incapacity began` IS A DATE @desc The day that incapacity began (any day otherwise)
      `the incapacity has ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that incapacity has ended
      `the day the incapacity ended` IS A DATE @desc The day the incapacity ended (any day otherwise)
      `I was a protected person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, during the incapacity, the injured person had a guardian (under the Guardianship Act 1987 or another law) or an order for management of their estate under the NSW Trustee and Guardian Act 2009 or the Guardianship Act 1987
      `the day of death` IS A DATE @desc For a claim by the estate or by relatives: the day the injured person died (any day otherwise)
      `the deceased could discover the claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a claim by the estate: whether the claim became discoverable by the person who died, before their death
      `the day the deceased could discover it` IS A DATE @desc The day the claim became discoverable by the person who died (any day otherwise)
      `the day of appointment` IS A DATE @desc For a claim by the estate: the day the personal representative (executor or administrator) was appointed (any day otherwise)
      `there was fraud or concealment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim is based on fraud or deceit by the person you sue, or that person fraudulently concealed the claim or who was liable
      `the day it was discovered` IS A DATE @desc The day you discovered the fraud, deceit or concealment, or could with reasonable diligence have discovered it (any day otherwise)
GIVETH A `Last day answer`
`By when must I commence my action` MEANS
    `the last day for` (`the facts from my answers` `my kind of claim` `who is suing` `the kind of abuse` `the day of the act or omission` `the injured person's date of birth` `the day the cause of action accrued` `the day the claim became discoverable by me` `the defendant was a parent or guardian or a close associate of one` `I had a capable parent or guardian while a minor` `I was incapacitated` `the day the incapacity began` `the incapacity has ended` `the day the incapacity ended` `I was a protected person` `the day of death` `the deceased could discover the claim` `the day the deceased could discover it` `the day of appointment` `there was fraud or concealment` `the day it was discovered`)

@export Was my action brought in time, or am I still in time to bring it (Limitation Act 1969 ss 6A, 14, 16-19, 50C-50F, 51, 52, 55)?
GIVEN `my kind of claim` IS A `Kind of claim` @desc The kind of claim: damages for death or personal injury (any disease or impairment of physical or mental condition, however the claim is framed); damages or money in contract (not under a deed) or tort with no personal injury, or money recoverable under an enactment; a claim founded on a deed; a claim on a judgment; a penalty or forfeiture recoverable under an enactment; a claim for which another Act fixes the limitation period, such as a motor accident claim; or another kind of claim
      `who is suing` IS A `Plaintiff` @desc Who brings the claim: the person injured or wronged, suing for themselves; the personal representative (executor or administrator) of an injured person who has died, suing for the estate; or relatives suing for the death under the Compensation to Relatives Act 1897
      `the kind of abuse` IS A `Kind of abuse` @desc If the injury resulted from abuse, its kind: sexual abuse; serious physical abuse; other abuse connected with sexual or serious physical abuse (by anyone), split by whether that sexual or serious physical abuse was also perpetrated before the 18th birthday; physical abuse that was not serious and not connected; other abuse not connected; or the injury did not result from abuse
      `the day of the act or omission` IS A DATE @desc The day of the act or omission that caused the injury or death (for abuse, the day it was perpetrated, or the first day if over a period); for another claim, the day of the breach or wrong
      `the injured person's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc The date of birth of the person who was injured or wronged (yours, if you sue for yourself)
      `the day the cause of action accrued` IS A DATE @desc For a claim outside Division 6 (an act or omission before 6 December 2002, or a claim that is not for personal injury): the day the cause of action accrued, usually the day the damage was suffered; for a judgment, the day it became enforceable (any day otherwise)
      `the day the claim became discoverable by me` IS A DATE @desc For a personal injury claim: the first day you knew or ought to have known that the injury or death had occurred, that it was caused by the defendant's fault, and (for injury) that it was serious enough to justify suing; for a minor with a capable parent or guardian, what that parent or guardian knew or ought to have known counts
      `the defendant was a parent or guardian or a close associate of one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, at the time of the act or omission, the person you sue was the injured person's parent or guardian, or someone so close to a parent or guardian that the parent might be influenced not to sue them, or the child might be unwilling to tell the parent about it
      `I had a capable parent or guardian while a minor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, while the injured person was under 18, they had a parent or guardian who was not themselves under a disability
      `I was incapacitated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, after the time began to run, the injured person was for 28 days or more in a row incapable of, or substantially impeded in, managing their affairs about this claim, because of disease or impairment, restraint (including detention) or war
      `the day the incapacity began` IS A DATE @desc The day that incapacity began (any day otherwise)
      `the incapacity has ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that incapacity has ended
      `the day the incapacity ended` IS A DATE @desc The day the incapacity ended (any day otherwise)
      `I was a protected person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, during the incapacity, the injured person had a guardian (under the Guardianship Act 1987 or another law) or an order for management of their estate under the NSW Trustee and Guardian Act 2009 or the Guardianship Act 1987
      `the day of death` IS A DATE @desc For a claim by the estate or by relatives: the day the injured person died (any day otherwise)
      `the deceased could discover the claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a claim by the estate: whether the claim became discoverable by the person who died, before their death
      `the day the deceased could discover it` IS A DATE @desc The day the claim became discoverable by the person who died (any day otherwise)
      `the day of appointment` IS A DATE @desc For a claim by the estate: the day the personal representative (executor or administrator) was appointed (any day otherwise)
      `there was fraud or concealment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim is based on fraud or deceit by the person you sue, or that person fraudulently concealed the claim or who was liable
      `the day it was discovered` IS A DATE @desc The day you discovered the fraud, deceit or concealment, or could with reasonable diligence have discovered it (any day otherwise)
      `I have brought the action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have already commenced the action in court
      `the day I brought it` IS A DATE @desc The day you commenced the action (any day otherwise)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A `Time limit answer`
`Was my action brought in time` MEANS
    `was the action brought in time` (`the facts from my answers` `my kind of claim` `who is suing` `the kind of abuse` `the day of the act or omission` `the injured person's date of birth` `the day the cause of action accrued` `the day the claim became discoverable by me` `the defendant was a parent or guardian or a close associate of one` `I had a capable parent or guardian while a minor` `I was incapacitated` `the day the incapacity began` `the incapacity has ended` `the day the incapacity ended` `I was a protected person` `the day of death` `the deceased could discover the claim` `the day the deceased could discover it` `the day of appointment` `there was fraud or concealment` `the day it was discovered`) `I have brought the action` `the day I brought it` `today`

§§ `Personal injury claims under Division 6 (an act or omission on or after 6 December 2002)`
-- Situation: your injury, or the death you sue for, was caused by an act or omission on or after 6 December 2002.

@export From what day does my personal injury claim count as discoverable (Limitation Act 1969 ss 50C(2), 50D, 50E)?
GIVEN `my kind of claim` IS A `Kind of claim` @desc The kind of claim: damages for death or personal injury (any disease or impairment of physical or mental condition, however the claim is framed); damages or money in contract (not under a deed) or tort with no personal injury, or money recoverable under an enactment; a claim founded on a deed; a claim on a judgment; a penalty or forfeiture recoverable under an enactment; a claim for which another Act fixes the limitation period, such as a motor accident claim; or another kind of claim
      `who is suing` IS A `Plaintiff` @desc Who brings the claim: the person injured or wronged, suing for themselves; the personal representative (executor or administrator) of an injured person who has died, suing for the estate; or relatives suing for the death under the Compensation to Relatives Act 1897
      `the kind of abuse` IS A `Kind of abuse` @desc If the injury resulted from abuse, its kind: sexual abuse; serious physical abuse; other abuse connected with sexual or serious physical abuse (by anyone), split by whether that sexual or serious physical abuse was also perpetrated before the 18th birthday; physical abuse that was not serious and not connected; other abuse not connected; or the injury did not result from abuse
      `the day of the act or omission` IS A DATE @desc The day of the act or omission that caused the injury or death (for abuse, the day it was perpetrated, or the first day if over a period); for another claim, the day of the breach or wrong
      `the injured person's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc The date of birth of the person who was injured or wronged (yours, if you sue for yourself)
      `the day the cause of action accrued` IS A DATE @desc For a claim outside Division 6 (an act or omission before 6 December 2002, or a claim that is not for personal injury): the day the cause of action accrued, usually the day the damage was suffered; for a judgment, the day it became enforceable (any day otherwise)
      `the day the claim became discoverable by me` IS A DATE @desc For a personal injury claim: the first day you knew or ought to have known that the injury or death had occurred, that it was caused by the defendant's fault, and (for injury) that it was serious enough to justify suing; for a minor with a capable parent or guardian, what that parent or guardian knew or ought to have known counts
      `the defendant was a parent or guardian or a close associate of one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, at the time of the act or omission, the person you sue was the injured person's parent or guardian, or someone so close to a parent or guardian that the parent might be influenced not to sue them, or the child might be unwilling to tell the parent about it
      `I had a capable parent or guardian while a minor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, while the injured person was under 18, they had a parent or guardian who was not themselves under a disability
      `I was incapacitated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, after the time began to run, the injured person was for 28 days or more in a row incapable of, or substantially impeded in, managing their affairs about this claim, because of disease or impairment, restraint (including detention) or war
      `the day the incapacity began` IS A DATE @desc The day that incapacity began (any day otherwise)
      `the incapacity has ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that incapacity has ended
      `the day the incapacity ended` IS A DATE @desc The day the incapacity ended (any day otherwise)
      `I was a protected person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, during the incapacity, the injured person had a guardian (under the Guardianship Act 1987 or another law) or an order for management of their estate under the NSW Trustee and Guardian Act 2009 or the Guardianship Act 1987
      `the day of death` IS A DATE @desc For a claim by the estate or by relatives: the day the injured person died (any day otherwise)
      `the deceased could discover the claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a claim by the estate: whether the claim became discoverable by the person who died, before their death
      `the day the deceased could discover it` IS A DATE @desc The day the claim became discoverable by the person who died (any day otherwise)
      `the day of appointment` IS A DATE @desc For a claim by the estate: the day the personal representative (executor or administrator) was appointed (any day otherwise)
      `there was fraud or concealment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim is based on fraud or deceit by the person you sue, or that person fraudulently concealed the claim or who was liable
      `the day it was discovered` IS A DATE @desc The day you discovered the fraud, deceit or concealment, or could with reasonable diligence have discovered it (any day otherwise)
GIVETH A `Discoverable answer`
`From when is my claim discoverable` MEANS
    `the discoverable answer for` (`the facts from my answers` `my kind of claim` `who is suing` `the kind of abuse` `the day of the act or omission` `the injured person's date of birth` `the day the cause of action accrued` `the day the claim became discoverable by me` `the defendant was a parent or guardian or a close associate of one` `I had a capable parent or guardian while a minor` `I was incapacitated` `the day the incapacity began` `the incapacity has ended` `the day the incapacity ended` `I was a protected person` `the day of death` `the deceased could discover the claim` `the day the deceased could discover it` `the day of appointment` `there was fraud or concealment` `the day it was discovered`)

@export Can the court extend my 12-year long-stop period, and to what day at most (Limitation Act 1969 ss 62A, 62F)?
GIVEN `my kind of claim` IS A `Kind of claim` @desc The kind of claim: damages for death or personal injury (any disease or impairment of physical or mental condition, however the claim is framed); damages or money in contract (not under a deed) or tort with no personal injury, or money recoverable under an enactment; a claim founded on a deed; a claim on a judgment; a penalty or forfeiture recoverable under an enactment; a claim for which another Act fixes the limitation period, such as a motor accident claim; or another kind of claim
      `who is suing` IS A `Plaintiff` @desc Who brings the claim: the person injured or wronged, suing for themselves; the personal representative (executor or administrator) of an injured person who has died, suing for the estate; or relatives suing for the death under the Compensation to Relatives Act 1897
      `the kind of abuse` IS A `Kind of abuse` @desc If the injury resulted from abuse, its kind: sexual abuse; serious physical abuse; other abuse connected with sexual or serious physical abuse (by anyone), split by whether that sexual or serious physical abuse was also perpetrated before the 18th birthday; physical abuse that was not serious and not connected; other abuse not connected; or the injury did not result from abuse
      `the day of the act or omission` IS A DATE @desc The day of the act or omission that caused the injury or death (for abuse, the day it was perpetrated, or the first day if over a period); for another claim, the day of the breach or wrong
      `the injured person's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc The date of birth of the person who was injured or wronged (yours, if you sue for yourself)
      `the day the cause of action accrued` IS A DATE @desc For a claim outside Division 6 (an act or omission before 6 December 2002, or a claim that is not for personal injury): the day the cause of action accrued, usually the day the damage was suffered; for a judgment, the day it became enforceable (any day otherwise)
      `the day the claim became discoverable by me` IS A DATE @desc For a personal injury claim: the first day you knew or ought to have known that the injury or death had occurred, that it was caused by the defendant's fault, and (for injury) that it was serious enough to justify suing; for a minor with a capable parent or guardian, what that parent or guardian knew or ought to have known counts
      `the defendant was a parent or guardian or a close associate of one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, at the time of the act or omission, the person you sue was the injured person's parent or guardian, or someone so close to a parent or guardian that the parent might be influenced not to sue them, or the child might be unwilling to tell the parent about it
      `I had a capable parent or guardian while a minor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, while the injured person was under 18, they had a parent or guardian who was not themselves under a disability
      `I was incapacitated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, after the time began to run, the injured person was for 28 days or more in a row incapable of, or substantially impeded in, managing their affairs about this claim, because of disease or impairment, restraint (including detention) or war
      `the day the incapacity began` IS A DATE @desc The day that incapacity began (any day otherwise)
      `the incapacity has ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that incapacity has ended
      `the day the incapacity ended` IS A DATE @desc The day the incapacity ended (any day otherwise)
      `I was a protected person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, during the incapacity, the injured person had a guardian (under the Guardianship Act 1987 or another law) or an order for management of their estate under the NSW Trustee and Guardian Act 2009 or the Guardianship Act 1987
      `the day of death` IS A DATE @desc For a claim by the estate or by relatives: the day the injured person died (any day otherwise)
      `the deceased could discover the claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a claim by the estate: whether the claim became discoverable by the person who died, before their death
      `the day the deceased could discover it` IS A DATE @desc The day the claim became discoverable by the person who died (any day otherwise)
      `the day of appointment` IS A DATE @desc For a claim by the estate: the day the personal representative (executor or administrator) was appointed (any day otherwise)
      `there was fraud or concealment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim is based on fraud or deceit by the person you sue, or that person fraudulently concealed the claim or who was liable
      `the day it was discovered` IS A DATE @desc The day you discovered the fraud, deceit or concealment, or could with reasonable diligence have discovered it (any day otherwise)
      `the court decides it is just and reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court decides that it is just and reasonable to extend the period, having regard to the delay and its reasons, prejudice to the defendant, the nature of your injury, the defendant's conduct, the advice you took, and when the claim was discoverable
GIVETH A `Long-stop extension answer`
`Can the court extend my long-stop period` MEANS
    `the s 62A answer for` (`the facts from my answers` `my kind of claim` `who is suing` `the kind of abuse` `the day of the act or omission` `the injured person's date of birth` `the day the cause of action accrued` `the day the claim became discoverable by me` `the defendant was a parent or guardian or a close associate of one` `I had a capable parent or guardian while a minor` `I was incapacitated` `the day the incapacity began` `the incapacity has ended` `the day the incapacity ended` `I was a protected person` `the day of death` `the deceased could discover the claim` `the day the deceased could discover it` `the day of appointment` `there was fraud or concealment` `the day it was discovered`) `if just and reasonable` `the court decides it is just and reasonable`

@export My parent or guardian failed to sue for me while I was a child: can the court extend my time (Limitation Act 1969 s 62D)?
GIVEN `my kind of claim` IS A `Kind of claim` @desc The kind of claim: damages for death or personal injury (any disease or impairment of physical or mental condition, however the claim is framed); damages or money in contract (not under a deed) or tort with no personal injury, or money recoverable under an enactment; a claim founded on a deed; a claim on a judgment; a penalty or forfeiture recoverable under an enactment; a claim for which another Act fixes the limitation period, such as a motor accident claim; or another kind of claim
      `who is suing` IS A `Plaintiff` @desc Who brings the claim: the person injured or wronged, suing for themselves; the personal representative (executor or administrator) of an injured person who has died, suing for the estate; or relatives suing for the death under the Compensation to Relatives Act 1897
      `the kind of abuse` IS A `Kind of abuse` @desc If the injury resulted from abuse, its kind: sexual abuse; serious physical abuse; other abuse connected with sexual or serious physical abuse (by anyone), split by whether that sexual or serious physical abuse was also perpetrated before the 18th birthday; physical abuse that was not serious and not connected; other abuse not connected; or the injury did not result from abuse
      `the day of the act or omission` IS A DATE @desc The day of the act or omission that caused the injury or death (for abuse, the day it was perpetrated, or the first day if over a period); for another claim, the day of the breach or wrong
      `the injured person's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc The date of birth of the person who was injured or wronged (yours, if you sue for yourself)
      `the day the cause of action accrued` IS A DATE @desc For a claim outside Division 6 (an act or omission before 6 December 2002, or a claim that is not for personal injury): the day the cause of action accrued, usually the day the damage was suffered; for a judgment, the day it became enforceable (any day otherwise)
      `the day the claim became discoverable by me` IS A DATE @desc For a personal injury claim: the first day you knew or ought to have known that the injury or death had occurred, that it was caused by the defendant's fault, and (for injury) that it was serious enough to justify suing; for a minor with a capable parent or guardian, what that parent or guardian knew or ought to have known counts
      `the defendant was a parent or guardian or a close associate of one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, at the time of the act or omission, the person you sue was the injured person's parent or guardian, or someone so close to a parent or guardian that the parent might be influenced not to sue them, or the child might be unwilling to tell the parent about it
      `I had a capable parent or guardian while a minor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, while the injured person was under 18, they had a parent or guardian who was not themselves under a disability
      `I was incapacitated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, after the time began to run, the injured person was for 28 days or more in a row incapable of, or substantially impeded in, managing their affairs about this claim, because of disease or impairment, restraint (including detention) or war
      `the day the incapacity began` IS A DATE @desc The day that incapacity began (any day otherwise)
      `the incapacity has ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that incapacity has ended
      `the day the incapacity ended` IS A DATE @desc The day the incapacity ended (any day otherwise)
      `I was a protected person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, during the incapacity, the injured person had a guardian (under the Guardianship Act 1987 or another law) or an order for management of their estate under the NSW Trustee and Guardian Act 2009 or the Guardianship Act 1987
      `the day of death` IS A DATE @desc For a claim by the estate or by relatives: the day the injured person died (any day otherwise)
      `the deceased could discover the claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a claim by the estate: whether the claim became discoverable by the person who died, before their death
      `the day the deceased could discover it` IS A DATE @desc The day the claim became discoverable by the person who died (any day otherwise)
      `the day of appointment` IS A DATE @desc For a claim by the estate: the day the personal representative (executor or administrator) was appointed (any day otherwise)
      `there was fraud or concealment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim is based on fraud or deceit by the person you sue, or that person fraudulently concealed the claim or who was liable
      `the day it was discovered` IS A DATE @desc The day you discovered the fraud, deceit or concealment, or could with reasonable diligence have discovered it (any day otherwise)
      `my parent's irrational decision caused the failure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court finds that the failure to sue in time is attributable to an irrational decision by your parent or guardian, made while you were a minor and after the claim was discoverable by them
      `there is evidence to establish my claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there is evidence to establish your cause of action, apart from any defence that the limitation period has expired
GIVETH A `Minor's extension answer`
`Can the court extend my time because my parent failed to sue` MEANS
    `the s 62D answer for` (`the facts from my answers` `my kind of claim` `who is suing` `the kind of abuse` `the day of the act or omission` `the injured person's date of birth` `the day the cause of action accrued` `the day the claim became discoverable by me` `the defendant was a parent or guardian or a close associate of one` `I had a capable parent or guardian while a minor` `I was incapacitated` `the day the incapacity began` `the incapacity has ended` `the day the incapacity ended` `I was a protected person` `the day of death` `the deceased could discover the claim` `the day the deceased could discover it` `the day of appointment` `there was fraud or concealment` `the day it was discovered`) `irrational decision` `my parent's irrational decision caused the failure` `evidence` `there is evidence to establish my claim`

§§ `What happens when the time runs out (Part 4 Division 1)`

@export What happens to my right to damages or money if my time runs out (Limitation Act 1969 ss 6A, 62F, 63)?
GIVEN `my kind of claim` IS A `Kind of claim` @desc The kind of claim: damages for death or personal injury (any disease or impairment of physical or mental condition, however the claim is framed); damages or money in contract (not under a deed) or tort with no personal injury, or money recoverable under an enactment; a claim founded on a deed; a claim on a judgment; a penalty or forfeiture recoverable under an enactment; a claim for which another Act fixes the limitation period, such as a motor accident claim; or another kind of claim
